    "C|第2、3集通过后转正：**Inner voice runs over action and stays short (TR-V09).** In conflict or fight shots the inner-voice line plays while the action continues; nobody stands still to \"listen\" to it, and a long line may be shortened to the novel's meaning (change dialogue, `<d>` and sub_shots together).": "C-002",
    "C|**Inner-voice (OS) shots follow the Inner-Monologue section above (handbook M33/M34; rewritten 2026-11-23).** Write the natural-close sentence at the start and `his lips stay naturally together` in the last hold sentence; the face reacts only with the eyes, brows, head and shoulders. Never add mouth or breath wording such as `lips remain completely closed`, `does not mouth the words` or `breath` — negated mouth words are errors too (M33 L647).": "C-003",
    "D|System voice — 系统声写进 `<d>`，由 H3 直出": "D-002",
    "F|Same-scene presence and costume lock — 同场在场人物入画 + 服装锁": "F-001",
    "F|**Hand props: write where the prop stays and where it never goes.** When a character holds anything that could go to the face (cup, glass, bottle, can, phone, cigarette, food, chopsticks), write its position for the whole shot, e.g. `she holds the cup at chest level the whole time; it never goes to her mouth`. If the story needs a sip or a call, write the exact second it is raised and when it comes down, and keep the mouth clear during any `<d>` line (see the dialogue-window section).": "F-006",
    "F|**No glasses unless the story gives a reason.** Write `no glasses` into each character's lock (the look / costume lock sentence). A character who wears glasses by design keeps the same pair in every shot (`wears the thin black-rimmed glasses from his reference`); glasses never appear, disappear or change mid-shot.": "F-007",
    "F|【待测】【分镜】【提示词】人物身份：小角色也写服装 ID 和性别（G01、G02，人物一致性）": "F-008",
