    "D|**System UI: short text on the panel; the system's full spoken line goes in `<d>` and H3 speaks it (TR-V04; Andy 11-23 17:27「系统声音在提示词里念完整内容」).**": "D-001",
    "F|**Face-state lock follows the story (TR-V01).** A visible story state on the face (tiredness, puffy eyelids, eye bags, a fresh look after a win) has a start beat and an end beat from the novel. Before the end beat every shot of that character writes the state; from the end beat on every shot writes the new state and binds the matching state image if an approved one exists. Never write the state in only some shots. Write the state by shape and degree only, never by colour or darkness words around the eyes (manual M50 item 2). Wrong: the tired face written in #3 and #9 only. Right: `<name>'s lower eyelids are puffy and swollen, with clear eye bags.` in every shot before the beat; `<name>'s face is fresh and rested; the lower eyelids are smooth.` in every shot after it.": "F-002",
    "F|**Prop size lock (TR-V03).** A prop whose reference is a multi-view or a sized sheet gets one fixed real-world size sentence in every shot it appears in: `The <prop> is <real-world size copied from the prop asset sheet> and it never grows or shrinks.`": "F-003",
    "F|**Adjacent-shot position lock (TR-V10).** Every shot of a scene states who is on which side of whom (also after a push, pull or hug). Only for two shots in the same scene where the action is continuous does the next shot open with `The characters keep the same left-right positions as in the previous shot.` followed by who is on which side. After a camera change, a jump cut or a time skip, write only who is on which side of whom in the new framing. Describe people's positions only; never write a sentence that locks the camera or the frame to the previous shot. Right (continuous push): #12 opens `The characters keep the same left-right positions as in the previous shot: Han Zixiao stays on screen-left of Jiang Che.` Right (#13 cuts to the reverse angle): `Han Zixiao is on Jiang Che's right, between him and the door.` Wrong: opening #13 with a sentence that ties its camera to the last frame of #12.": "F-004",
    "F|**Every shot binds a scene (TR-V12).** `scene_ids` is never empty. Same-scene shots share one scene sentence (F-001 item 14).": "F-005",
    "F|**Adjacent-shot position lock (TR-V10).** Every shot of a scene states who is on which side of whom (also after a push, pull or hug). Only for two shots in the same scene where the action is continuous does the next shot open with `The characters keep the same left-right positions as in the previous shot.` followed by who is on which side. After a camera change, a jump cut or a time skip, write only who is on which side of whom in the new framing. Describe people's positions only; never write a sentence that locks the camera or the frame to the previous shot. Right (continuous push): #12 opens `The characters keep the same left-right positions as in the previous shot: <A> stays on screen-left of <B>.` Right (#13 cuts to the reverse angle): `<A> is on <B>'s right, between him and the door.` Wrong: opening #13 with a sentence that ties its camera to the last frame of #12.": "F-004",
